<title>SRI LANKA: Weather-Monsoon seen breaking over Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather-Monsoon seen breaking over Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Wednesday morning</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Bowathenna		0</p>
<p>    Canyon		    0</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	     0</p>
<p>    Kotmale		   0</p>
<p>    Laxapana		  0</p>
<p>    Moussakele		0</p>
<p>    Norton		    0</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0</p>
<p>    Victoria		  0</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	    0</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		   0</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  0</p>
<p>The department said weak southwest monsoonal conditions are gradually developing over the island and forecast showers in the Central, Sabaragamuwa and Western provinces and in the Galle and Matara districts with afternoon or evening thunder showers in the Eastern and Uva provinces.</p>
</text>
